  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The Pronouns is an iconic collection of dance-instruction poems from 1964 by performance artist, composer, anarchist-pacifist, and poet Jackson Mac Low, who was famous for employing techniques of "systematic chance" in his writing. Each poem uses one of forty pronouns and a random combination of a limited vocabulary to create a script that one or more dancers interpret, thereby bringing the poem to life differently each time it is read or performed"-- Provided by publisher.</subfield>
  </datafield>
